purpose: Paradigm Conductor — workspace manager + multimodal mission control for Claude Code sessions + Symphony inter-agent messaging
version: 0.6.0
description: Workspace manager that launches and owns CC instances. Shared camera architecture — single AVCaptureSession feeds both gaze and gesture Vision providers simultaneously. Video/voice toggle controls with keyboard shortcuts. Eyebrow-triggered voice control, custom gesture recording, voice command binding, gaze-to-grid zone targeting, and Paradigm context enrichment. Targeted terminal close (per-window, not kill-all). Native macOS Swift/SwiftUI app launched via paradigm conductor CLI command. Single-owner architecture — AppDelegate owns orchestrator and workspace lifecycle. Symphony Phase 1-2: auto-detects CC sessions, registers agent parts in The Score (~/.paradigm/score/), relays notes on 5s poll, file approval with trust config, thread list view, file request notification, and Symphony settings tab.
context:
  - Native macOS Swift/SwiftUI app
  - Ships via paradigm conductor CLI command
  - 7 platform abstraction protocols for future Windows port
  - All ML inference runs locally — zero cloud, zero cost, no Python dependency
  - SharedCameraSession distributes frames to gaze + gesture providers simultaneously
  - VisionGazeProvider uses VNDetectFaceLandmarksRequest for native gaze + eyebrow tracking
  - Sidebar-based workspace manager replaces floating overlay
  - Custom gesture recording via DTW matching
  - Voice command phrase binding with fuzzy matching
  - Single-owner pattern — AppDelegate is the sole lifecycle owner of orchestrator and workspace
  - Video/voice toggle icons in header bar with Cmd+Shift+V / Cmd+Shift+M hotkeys
  - Targeted terminal close via AppleScript window IDs — closing one window no longer kills all terminals
  - Symphony: file-based inter-agent messaging at ~/.paradigm/score/ with JSONL mailboxes
  - Symphony: auto-link creates agent parts when CC sessions are detected
  - Symphony: 5s relay poll routes notes between agent inboxes/outboxes
  - Symphony: file approval with trust.yaml, hard-deny patterns, SHA-256 hashing

# ============================================
# Components (#)
# ============================================

